                  "content": "The API will follow RESTful principles and utilize JSON for data exchange.  API versioning will be implemented (`/api/v1/...`). Authentication will be handled via Sanctum. Key endpoints include:\n\n*   **Users:** `/api/v1/users`, `/api/v1/users/{id}`, `/api/v1/profile` (for authenticated user)\n*   **Skills:** `/api/v1/skills`, `/api/v1/skills/{id}`, `/api/v1/categories`, `/api/v1/categories/{id}`\n*   **Sessions:** `/api/v1/sessions`, `/api/v1/sessions/{id}`, `/api/v1/sessions/{id}/confirm`, `/api/v1/sessions/{id}/cancel`\n*   **Reviews:** `/api/v1/reviews`, `/api/v1/reviews/{id}`\n*   **Payment Transactions:** `/api/v1/payment-transactions`, `/api/v1/payment-transactions/{id}`\n*   **Chat Messages:** `/api/v1/chat-messages`, `/api/v1/chat-messages/{session_id}` (using websockets for real-time updates)\n*   **Notifications:** `/api/v1/notifications`, `/api/v1/notifications/{id}/mark-as-read`\n\nAll endpoints will implement proper authorization checks using Laravel's policies.",
