                "auth_flow": {
                  "content": "Authentication will be handled using Laravel Sanctum, providing a lightweight and secure API authentication system.\n\n1.  **Registration/Login:** Users register/login via standard forms.  The backend authenticates the user and issues an API token (Sanctum).\n2.  **API Requests:** Subsequent API requests include the token in the `Authorization` header (`Bearer {token}`).\n3.  **Authentication:** The backend uses Sanctum to authenticate the user based on the token.\n4.  **Authorization:** Laravel Policies will be used to control access to resources based on user roles and permissions.  For example, a policy might ensure that only the teacher can confirm a session.\n5.  **Password Reset:** Standard Laravel password reset functionality.\n\nTwo-factor authentication (2FA) will be implemented using packages like `laravel-2fa` [https://github.com/antonioribeiro/laravel-2fa] and integrated using webauthn, as defined by the W3C [https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-2/], for better user experience.",
